      "code": "double_quoted_string = \"\\\"\" ( [^\"]* ) >{ str_start = fpc; } %{ str_len = fpc - str_start; } \"\\\"\";",
      "note": "First project-code parser action that materializes the attacker-controlled quoted value into the start pointer and length used by the vulnerable copy helper.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "readstat/src/txt/readstat_copy.c",
      "function": "readstat_copy_quoted",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (this_len >= buf_len) {\n        this_len = buf_len;\n    }",
      "note": "When the caller passes a 1024-byte quoted string into a 1024-byte destination, this branch leaves `this_len == buf_len == 1024`. The loop can therefore consume the entire destination, and the later terminator write has no in-bounds slot left. The missing obligation is the same one already implemented in `readstat_copy()`: cap at `buf_len - 1` before writing `\\0`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
